(formerly RTX Transcode Engine) distribution that carries the SPDX license expression

    GPL-3.0-or-later WITH Plugin-Exception

(collectively, the "Covered Work").  The name "Plugin-Exception" (also referred
to as "CineRTX Plugin-Exception") refers to this document.

0. DEFINITIONS

"Plugin Interface" means the pure C application binary interface declared in
include/shim/rtx_shim_abi.h, include/shim/ngx_bridge_abi.h and
include/shim/fruc_bridge_abi.h, together with the loader-facing backend
interface declared in include/rtx/backend.h and include/shim/i_engine_backend.h,
as distributed with the Covered Work.

"Independent Module" means a software component that

  (a) is not derived from the Covered Work;
  (b) is distributed under license terms other than the GPLv3, including
      proprietary end-user license terms; and
  (c) is combined with the Covered Work only at run time by dynamic loading
      through the Plugin Interface, without being statically linked into, or
      compiled together with, the Covered Work.

NVIDIA CUDA, the Video Codec SDK (NVDEC/NVENC), the Optical Flow SDK
(NvOFFRUC), TensorRT, and the RTX Video SDK (NGX, including standalone plugin
bridge modules such as rtx_ngx_bridge.dll that may internally link vendor
static stub libraries such as nvsdk_ngx_s.lib) are examples of Independent
Modules.  The same applies to optical flow frame rate up-conversion bridge
modules such as rtx_fruc_bridge.dll that may internally link vendor stub
libraries (NvOFFRUC, nvinfer, nvonnxparser) while exporting only the pure C
ABI of include/shim/fruc_bridge_abi.h to the Covered Work.

The statically linked, surgically trimmed FFmpeg archives
(libavformat/libavcodec/libavutil/libswresample, built without --enable-gpl and
without --enable-nonfree and therefore under LGPLv2.1-or-later) are NOT
Independent Modules: they are combined into the Covered Work at build time
under LGPLv2.1 section 3, which permits the relicensing of the combined work
under the GPLv3 as modified by this exception.

1. ADDITIONAL PERMISSION

You may convey the Covered Work, in source or object form, combined with
Independent Modules, and distribute the resulting combination, without the
Independent Modules being treated as part of, or as derivative works of, the
Covered Work, provided that:

  (a) the Covered Work remains licensed under the GPLv3 as modified by this
      exception;

  (b) every Independent Module is combined only at run time through the
      Plugin Interface and is not statically linked into the Covered Work;

  (c) the distribution does not include NVIDIA SDK headers, import libraries,
      static libraries, or other proprietary SDK material as part of the
      Covered Work's source code; and

  (d) recipients are informed that the Independent Modules are governed by
      their own license terms and are not covered by this exception.

2. NO EFFECT ON OTHER TERMS

This exception does not grant any license or other right to any Independent
Module, and it does not alter the terms under which any Independent Module is
distributed.  It does not permit combining the Covered Work with any component
in a way that would make the Covered Work, or any portion of it, subject to
the terms of a proprietary license.

3. TERMINATION

If you modify the Covered Work so that it statically links, or is otherwise
combined at build time with, an Independent Module, this exception does not
apply to that modified work, and the GPLv3 applies to the combination without
this additional permission.

